WEBVTT

00:02.840 --> 00:07.640
The will was sent back to the capital Xie Xuan was ordered to assist in governance.

00:07.720 --> 00:12.920
Crown Prince Sikong Sheng successfully ascended the throne posthumously titled you as Emperor Xuancheng.

00:13.280 --> 00:16.613
And changed the era name to Taian the following year.

00:27.920 --> 00:32.040
After Sikong Sheng ascended the throne although nominally the ruler of all under heaven.

00:32.120 --> 00:37.960
The army still had many remnants of Sikong Xu's faction threatening the state's stability.

00:38.880 --> 00:43.000
Grand General Zhu Yuanzhi, in the name of intimidating border tribes.

00:43.280 --> 00:46.840
Stationed troops at the Yan Bei border regarding this.

00:46.920 --> 00:52.560
Sikong Sheng adopted a strategy of divide and conquer on one hand forgiving the past.

00:52.960 --> 00:58.600
And giving rewards to all on the other hand for those who repeatedly disobeyed court orders.

00:58.760 --> 01:00.640
Carrying out targeted punishment.

01:02.280 --> 01:07.680
Although this was effective many of the Prince of Yan's former subordinates, though appearing to submit.

01:07.760 --> 01:13.560
Still harbored resentment in their hearts and after Zhu Yuanzhi was summoned to the capital and given a nominal position.

01:13.640 --> 01:15.600
Became even more closely connected.

01:16.480 --> 01:22.440
The fourth year of Taian Sikong Sheng, in the name of returning to the old capital wished to move the capital to Yong'an.

01:22.520 --> 01:27.800
Moving the political center north met with fierce opposition from Zhu Yuanzhi.

01:27.880 --> 01:31.640
United with old friends, noble families, and scholar clans finally forced to abandon the plan.

01:33.000 --> 01:48.000
During his reign, he instituted imperial examinations, reformed military systems, and established new laws. Though unable to completely eradicate aristocratic influence, he brought peace and prosperity to the Taian era, remembered by posterity as the 'Rule of Taian'.

